{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Henry Bayliss, a brilliant redneck scientist deep in the Louisiana bayou, is up to <i>something</i>. Enter <strong>Jack Briar:</strong>\u00a0the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms' best agent, and the natural choice for this kind of field work. But Creepy Redneck Dinosaur Mansion 3 was cancelled! What's Jack Briar even <i>doing</i> here?!<br><br>Join Jack Briar as he races to prevent the Bayliss disaster, explores a creepy mansion, and defeats anyone who gets in his way. Look out dinos, cause you\u2019re gonna get jur<i>ass</i>-kic'd!</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>What is this?</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A match-3, metroidvania, narrative sequel to Creepy Redneck Dinosaur Mansion 3.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore the Bayliss mansion as Jack Briar, earn Traits by exploring, and use those Traits to unlock new paths.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A faithful follow-up from Pedalboard Games, headed by CRDM3's co-lead.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A direct sequel with more puzzles, returning characters, new characters, and a whole lot more meta-commentary on game development.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A brand new soundtrack, a new protagonist, and new mysteries to unravel.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The first entry in Strange Scaffold's Project Share program, allowing Pedalboard Games to leverage the original game's codebase. </p></li></ul>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3830150?t=1758635848","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3830150/8568d217ea7fb61f38be4c21282ffa4984320a6d/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1758635848","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3830150/0c85628bcbec765c391f1b7890b644d806f1f773/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1758635848","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3830150/0c85628bcbec765c391f1b7890b644d806f1f773/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1758635848","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Partial Controller Support","id":18},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[5],"notes":"Profanity used by some characters. Deals with themes of loss, death, and terminal illness."},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Henry Bayliss, a brilliant redneck scientist deep in the Louisiana bayou, is up to <i>something</i>. Enter <strong>Jack Briar:</strong>\u00a0the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms' best agent, and the natural choice for this kind of field work. But Creepy Redneck Dinosaur Mansion 3 was cancelled! What's Jack Briar even <i>doing</i> here?!<br><br>Join Jack Briar as he races to prevent the Bayliss disaster, explores a creepy mansion, and defeats anyone who gets in his way. Look out dinos, cause you\u2019re gonna get jur<i>ass</i>-kic'd!</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>What is this?</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A match-3, metroidvania, narrative sequel to Creepy Redneck Dinosaur Mansion 3.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore the Bayliss mansion as Jack Briar, earn Traits by exploring, and use those Traits to unlock new paths.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A faithful follow-up from Pedalboard Games, headed by CRDM3's co-lead.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A direct sequel with more puzzles, returning characters, new characters, and a whole lot more meta-commentary on game development.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A brand new soundtrack, a new protagonist, and new mysteries to unravel.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The first entry in Strange Scaffold's Project Share program, allowing Pedalboard Games to leverage the original game's codebase. </p></li></ul>","developers":["Pedalboard Games"],"genres":[{"description":"Adventure","id":"25"},{"descript